  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Amentum Services' federal contracting activity in FY2026 to date shows $2.4B in obligations across 338 awards, with an average award size of $7.2M. Obligations fell 31.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.5B, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $708M. Major NAICS markets for Amentum Services this year include Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $846M and Security Guards and Patrol Services at $506M. Engineering Services and Facilities Support Services are also significant, with $253M and $232M respectively. The vendor recorded obligations in a mix of services and manufacturing markets, including Computer Facilities Management Services at $125M and Aircraft Manufacturing at $91M. Historical obligations show a rise into FY24 at $3.8B and FY25 at $3.5B before the current-year FY26 total of $2.4B. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date contract obligations rather than full-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How much is Amentum Services selling to the government this fiscal year?",
        "body": "Amentum Services has $2.4B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 31.2% year over year. The firm has 338 awards so far with an average award size of $7.2M. Historical context shows FY25 obligations at $3.5B and FY24 obligations at $3.8B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Amentum Services' biggest federal customers and which markets drive those sales?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.5B and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $708M in FY2026 to date. Top markets by obligation are Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $846M and Security Guards and Patrol Services at $506M. Engineering Services and Facilities Support Services contribute $253M and $232M respectively, with Computer Facilities Management Services at $125M and Aircraft Manufacturing at $91M."
      }
    ]
  },
